s3-2-p2 = prose (cons "There are at least three relations worth keeping distinct. Two expressions may be definitionally equal because they reduce to the same expression under the calculus. They may be propositionally equal because an inhabitant of their identity type is constructed. They may be observationally indistinguishable under some chosen experiment even when no equality of their complete structures has been established." nil)
